  -C, --dir <DIR>  Run in a different directory

=== tk mv ===
Move a task to a different project

(Deliberate break from the Go version: `mv` moves tasks only. Renaming a whole
project lives under `config project rename`.)

Usage: tk mv <SOURCE> <PROJECT>

Arguments:
  <SOURCE>   Task ID or ref
  <PROJECT>  Target project name

Flags:
  -h, --help       Print help

Global flags:
  -j, --json       Output as JSON
  -C, --dir <DIR>  Run in a different directory

=== tk clean ===
Remove old completed tasks

Usage: tk clean [--older-than <OLDER_THAN>] [--force]

Flags:
      --older-than <OLDER_THAN>  Remove tasks completed more than N days ago
      --force                    Force clean even if disabled in config
  -h, --help                     Print help

Global flags:
  -j, --json                     Output as JSON
  -C, --dir <DIR>                Run in a different directory

